rchives","Health programs administration and funding","Internet, web applications, social media","Medical research","National Institutes of Health (NIH)","Neurological disorders","Public-private cooperation","Research administration and funding"],"sponsorBioguideId":"Q000023","cosponsorCount":102,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8205","industries":[{"industry":"pharma","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"The bill directly funds research grants and regulatory pathways for development of drugs and therapies targeting ALS and neurodegenerative diseases."},{"industry":"health-providers","confidence":0.4,"rationale":"Providers treating ALS patients may see changes in available investigational therapies and clinical trial access, though the bill focuses primarily on research and regulatory processes."}],"plainSummary":"This bill extends funding through fiscal year 2031 for federal programs that support research and development of treatments for ALS (Lou Gehrig's disease) and similar neurodegenerative diseases. It requires the National Institutes of Health to track safety data on experimental drugs and mandates that the Food and Drug Administration publish a five-year plan describing how it will help develop and approve therapies for these rare diseases. The bill also continues a public-private partnership between federal agencies and outside organizations working on neurodegenerative disease treatments.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People with an illness that is still being studied. Anyone who uses the internet.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"B001257","score":0.0756937925283595},"overlapCount":102},"meaning":{"percentile":50.812430982804855,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.6022279722883243}}],"votes":[{"id":"a64a90b759595d68f3a8d502","billId":"119-hr-7008","date":"2026-07-22T16:51:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result